WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.230
Stop me if you've heard this one before.

00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:07.471
A young man was driving home from work late
one rainy night when he spotted a woman in

00:00:07.471 --> 00:00:11.579
a white dress and a red sweater walking along
the shoulder of the road.

00:00:11.579 --> 00:00:15.919
Concerned for her safety, he slowed down and
rolled down the window so he could talk to

00:00:15.919 --> 00:00:16.919
her.

00:00:16.919 --> 00:00:20.590
When he asked where she was going, she said
she was walking to her parents' house.

00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:23.699
The man pulled over and offered her a ride
that she accepted.

00:00:23.699 --> 00:00:28.420
The woman gave him the address of her home,
hopped in the backseat, and the man drove

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:29.420
off.

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:32.610
He sensed that she must've been cold from
walking in the rain, so he cranked up the

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:35.100
car's heater to help her dry off.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:39.030
Soon she removed her heavy red sweater and
placed it on the seat next to her.

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:43.550
The man tried to make friendly conversation
- asking if the woman had a job, what she

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:48.649
was studying at school, where she'd been that
day - but she remained quiet, staring out

00:00:48.649 --> 00:00:49.850
the window.

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:52.719
Until they drove past an old graveyard.

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:57.360
The woman began pounding on the glass of the
car as if she desperately wanted something.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:02.219
Unsure of what to do, the man pulled over,
but before he could ask her what was happening

00:01:02.219 --> 00:01:04.059
she had gotten out of the car.

00:01:04.059 --> 00:01:09.240
He exited the car to try and find her but
the woman was nowhere to be seen.

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:11.090
She must have somehow ran off.

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:14.630
Confused, the man got back in his car and
drove away.

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:19.130
He went on his way and didn’t think of it
again until the next day, when he noticed

00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:22.140
her sweater was still in the back of his car.

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:26.579
He decided to go to the house she had originally
given him the address for and give it back

00:01:26.579 --> 00:01:27.579
to her.

00:01:27.579 --> 00:01:31.520
He found the home without any trouble, but
when he knocked on the door the old woman

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:34.400
who answered it was confused by his story.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:38.570
She told him that her daughter couldn't have
possibly left her sweater in his car, because

00:01:38.570 --> 00:01:42.240
she'd died in a car accident 30 years ago.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:46.600
The vanishing hitchhiker is a classic ghost
story, with the details varying from place

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:49.740
to place and storyteller to storyteller.

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:54.869
In Chicago, she goes by Resurrection Mary,
named after the graveyard she asks for rides

00:01:54.869 --> 00:01:55.869
to.

00:01:55.869 --> 00:02:02.119
In Okinawa, Japan, she's known as the Nightwalker
of Nago, and she only appears to taxi drivers.

00:02:02.119 --> 00:02:07.250
In Kent, England, she's Suzanne, a bride killed
in a car wreck on the way to her bachelorette

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:08.250
party.

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:12.060
In North Carolina, her name is Lydia, and
in Hawaii she's believed to be the goddess

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:14.360
Pele in human form.

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:19.010
But as far as our friends at the SCP Foundation
are concerned, the vanishing hitchhiker's

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:24.790
name is Mary Talish, also known as SCP-1337.

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:30.440
On the 19th of May, 1952, college sophomore
Mary Talish was abducted on her way to class

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:32.920
in her hometown of Muncie, Indiana.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:36.980
When police found her body 2 weeks later,
her eyes and heart had been torn from her

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:41.970
body in a ritualistic fashion, and she had
scrapes and bruises that suggested she'd been

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:43.630
beaten before her murder.

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:49.030
Her killers were never caught, and her body
was returned to her family for burial in Tomlinson

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:50.230
Cemetery.

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:55.850
Starting on the 19th of June that same year,
someone matching Mary's description - a caucasian

00:02:55.850 --> 00:03:02.010
woman with blonde hair, standing 150 cm tall
and wearing a red sweater - was spotted trying

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:06.120
to flag down passing vehicles along Mayflower
Road.

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:11.610
Since then, every month, on the 19th, Mary
has been sighted along that stretch of road,

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:15.120
and every month, the same scenario plays out.

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:19.620
Mary gives anyone who picks her up directions
to her parents' house, then on the way, she

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:23.250
instructs the driver to stop at the graveyard
where she was buried.

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:26.220
She vanishes from the car, leaving her sweater.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:30.090
The driver of the car tries to return the
sweater to her parents' house, only to be

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:32.070
told that Mary Talish was dead.

00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:36.700
When the SCP foundation was made aware of
Mary Talish's pattern of haunting in the late

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:41.820
50's, they set up a system where agents would
patrol Mayflower Road at hourly intervals

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:44.650
with the intention of picking Mary up.

00:03:44.650 --> 00:03:49.660
Agents were sent on their own in non-Foundation
cars and instructed to stick to the accepted

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:54.540
script of the vanishing hitchhiker legend,
without attempting to engage Mary in further

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:55.900
conversation.

00:03:55.900 --> 00:03:59.860
Mary's parents were also given E-class Agent
status to keep them from speaking out about

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:04.580
the haunting, and told that the Foundation
was working on a way to set the spirit to

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:05.580
rest.

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:10.380
Early attempts to study the apparition were
inconclusive - it proved impossible for the

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:14.940
Foundation to relocate her or trigger her
manifestation outside of the 19th of every

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:19.549
month, and attempts to analyze her sweater
were fruitless, since if the sweater wasn't

00:04:19.549 --> 00:04:24.370
returned to the Talish family home it would
simply vanish from containment at or around

00:04:24.370 --> 00:04:27.190
sunset on the next 19th.

00:04:27.190 --> 00:04:32.750
For 20 years, SCP-1337 events continued to
happen as normal.

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:36.830
D-Class personnel under the instruction of
the Foundation would pick Mary up, drive her

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:40.220
past the cemetery, and return her sweater
to her parents.

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:45.410
It was business as usual, and in fact, it
was one of the more sedate recurring apparitions

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:47.660
the Foundation had to deal with.

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:52.500
But, as you might have guessed, that peace
wouldn't last forever.

00:04:52.500 --> 00:05:00.060
Enter Dr. Lawson - who, in 1972, was placed
in charge of all resources regarding SCP-1337.

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:05.810
Dr. Lawson was getting sick of all this phantom
hitchhiker business, and while most of the

00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:09.780
Foundation was happy to keep this routine
going, Lawson thought that the continual picking

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:14.620
up and dropping off of Mary Talish and her
red sweater was a waste of the Foundation’s

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:16.130
valuable time.

00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:21.690
After all, it was the early 70's - the price
of oil was at an all-time high, so the expense

00:05:21.690 --> 00:05:27.260
of sending car after car up and down the same
road for a solid day once a month just to

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:30.570
pick up a ghost was more trouble than it was
worth.

00:05:30.570 --> 00:05:35.700
So, Lawson started developing a plan, one
that he didn't go through the proper Foundation

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:37.260
channels to approve.

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:42.620
He reasoned that the reason Mary's ghost kept
coming back was because she wanted something.

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:46.210
Since always asked for a ride home, then it
must mean that she wanted to return back to

00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:47.210
her parents.

00:05:47.210 --> 00:05:53.810
So, logic followed that if she had nothing,
or no one, to go back to then she'd stop appearing.

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:59.770
On 18th June, 1973, Lawson went ahead with
his plan without his superiors' knowledge

00:05:59.770 --> 00:06:04.980
and ordered the execution of Mary Talish's
parents, as well as the immediate demolition

00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:06.639
of their family home.

00:06:06.639 --> 00:06:11.680
According to his journals, Lawson had hoped
that his attempt at decommissioning 1337 would

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:16.820
significantly cut the Foundation's gas bills,
freeing up valuable funds, at which point

00:06:16.820 --> 00:06:20.270
he'd surely be promoted in 'recognition of
his brilliance'.

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:22.820
But that wasn't what happened.

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:28.139
Lawson was demoted from team leader to junior
staff, and only kept on 1337 detail out of

00:06:28.139 --> 00:06:33.250
the belief that, without a family to return
to, Lawson would become the new focal point

00:06:33.250 --> 00:06:36.170
of the haunting should Mary Talish ever return.

00:06:36.170 --> 00:06:41.420
Though Lawson's actions weren't at all above
board, even by SCP Foundation standards, they

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:43.050
did seem to have worked.

00:06:43.050 --> 00:06:46.770
The 19th of June came and went without a single
Mary sighting.

00:06:46.770 --> 00:06:48.610
And she wasn't seen the next month either.

00:06:48.610 --> 00:06:53.300
A full year went by without any sign of the
Mayflower Road apparition.

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:58.410
Satisfied with this turn of events, the Foundation
made the decision to officially reclassify

00:06:58.410 --> 00:07:04.560
SCP-1337 from “Safe” to “Safe Decommissioned”
and the gas money that was budgeted for the

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:09.880
Mayflower Road patrol was redirected to the
SCP-682 tank acid fund.

00:07:09.880 --> 00:07:15.860
But even though everything seemed to have
been sorted out, Lawson wasn't entirely satisfied.

00:07:15.860 --> 00:07:17.919
And just because of his demotion.

00:07:17.919 --> 00:07:23.150
Whether it was intuition or merely guilt-induced
paranoia is unclear, but he suspected that

00:07:23.150 --> 00:07:25.490
Mary was still out there somewhere.

00:07:25.490 --> 00:07:29.580
At first he thought that she might show up
on the anniversary of her parents' deaths,

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:34.889
but then that date came and went, as did eight
more anniversaries after it.

00:07:34.889 --> 00:07:40.790
Finally, on the 19th of June, 1983, Lawson
decided he had to see for himself.

00:07:40.790 --> 00:07:45.870
Fitted with recording equipment, he drove
alone, in a non-Foundation standard car, down

00:07:45.870 --> 00:07:51.160
that lonely stretch of road where so many
before him had stopped to pick up that mysterious

00:07:51.160 --> 00:07:53.370
blonde woman with the red sweater.

00:07:53.370 --> 00:07:58.280
He had to prove to himself that she wouldn't
show up, that he had really and truly gotten

00:07:58.280 --> 00:07:59.960
rid of her for good.

00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:03.350
It was about 5 o'clock in the evening when
he reached Mayflower Road.

00:08:03.350 --> 00:08:06.490
At first, he didn't experience anything strange.

00:08:06.490 --> 00:08:11.570
He scanned the roadside, looking for the phantom
hitchhiker walking along it, but there was

00:08:11.570 --> 00:08:12.580
nobody there.

00:08:12.580 --> 00:08:17.540
Dr. Lawson breathed a sigh of relief - he
may have orchestrated the deaths of two innocent

00:08:17.540 --> 00:08:20.330
people, but at least it hadn't been for nothing.

00:08:20.330 --> 00:08:25.210
He turned on the recorder he'd brought with
him and logged that nothing had happened.

00:08:25.210 --> 00:08:28.560
SCP-1337 had been permanently neutralized.

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:32.700
As he approached the t-intersection and prepared
to turn onto Marsh Avenue, he looked up to

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:34.430
adjust his rear view mirror.

00:08:34.430 --> 00:08:40.070
To his horror, he found that he wasn't alone
in the car - someone was in the seat behind

00:08:40.070 --> 00:08:43.729
him, someone with blonde hair and a red sweater.

00:08:43.729 --> 00:08:48.480
His last transmission consisted only of “Wait,
who the hell are yo-“, before the recording

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:50.200
abruptly stopped.

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:53.760
Lawson's car was found soon after by Foundation
agents.

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:57.960
Lawson was dead in the front seat, bruised
and bloody, with his eyes and heart ripped

00:08:57.960 --> 00:09:00.490
out in a ritualistic fashion.

00:09:00.490 --> 00:09:05.550
Just the way Mary Talish had been found all
the way back in 1952.

00:09:05.550 --> 00:09:09.080
It turns out that Mary hadn't been neutralized
after all.

00:09:09.080 --> 00:09:14.440
She'd just been waiting for a chance to get
revenge on the man who killed her family.

00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:16.780
And Mary didn't stop with Dr. Lawson.

00:09:16.780 --> 00:09:21.390
No longer does she appear, walking along the
road waiting for someone to offer her a ride

00:09:21.390 --> 00:09:23.520
before disappearing without incident.

00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:28.300
Now, should someone pass by without offering
a ride, she will appear in their backseat

00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:31.589
before re-enacting the method of her own death
upon the driver.

00:09:31.589 --> 00:09:34.860
And her physical appearance has changed too.

00:09:34.860 --> 00:09:38.940
Whereas before she looked like the image of
the pretty young woman before her tragedy,

00:09:38.940 --> 00:09:43.360
now recordings show that she appears with
the wounds of her death present, her eyes

00:09:43.360 --> 00:09:49.190
gouged out of their sockets and a massive
hole in her chest where her heart should be.

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:52.730
The same wounds she inflicts on her victims.

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:57.600
The SCP Foundation has tried closing off and
even destroying the road, but that has only

00:09:57.600 --> 00:10:02.730
resulted in Mary manifesting at other locations
in and around Muncie.

00:10:02.730 --> 00:10:06.400
Foundation documents reveal that any back
road in the city can potentially serve as

00:10:06.400 --> 00:10:12.350
host to a 1337 event, and all attempts to
contain the apparition have failed.

00:10:12.350 --> 00:10:17.080
The only way someone who has seen Mary can
avoid her wrath is by stopping to pick her

00:10:17.080 --> 00:10:21.880
up, at which point she will de-materialize
before reappearing on another road.

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:27.370
Mobile Task Forces have been unsuccessful,
as Mary only appears to those driving alone,

00:10:27.370 --> 00:10:31.450
and all agents who have been sent on solo
missions to apprehend her have resulted in

00:10:31.450 --> 00:10:33.700
the death of the agent.

00:10:33.700 --> 00:10:38.649
SCP-1337 was reinstated, this time as Euclid
class.

00:10:38.649 --> 00:10:44.440
Currently, the foundation's method of managing
SCP-1337 is to dispatch a security team on

00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:49.160
the 19th of every month to monitor all of
the places where a potential sighting could

00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:50.420
take place.

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:55.420
As soon as signs of a manifestation are identified,
a remotely controlled vehicle containing a

00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:58.330
single D-class is driven to the location.

00:10:58.330 --> 00:11:03.970
Once Mary appears in the car, the car is piloted
to the empty lot where her home used to stand,

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:07.710
and the remains of the D-class are then disposed
of.

00:11:07.710 --> 00:11:13.279
Like a lot of stories that get passed down
as urban legends, the story of SCP-1337 has

00:11:13.279 --> 00:11:15.600
a lesson that can be taken away from it.

00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:21.770
This SCP started off as an ordinary local
haunting, no more deadly than Lydia, Suzanne,

00:11:21.770 --> 00:11:26.850
Resurrection Mary, or any of the countless
other local versions of the vanishing hitchhiker

00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:27.850
story.

00:11:27.850 --> 00:11:32.020
But, thanks to one rogue Foundation doctor
and his desire to rush to what he thought

00:11:32.020 --> 00:11:37.279
would be an efficient solution, the spirit
not only became harder to control but also

00:11:37.279 --> 00:11:42.680
much more violent and bloodthirsty than anyone
was prepared to deal with.

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:47.820
So, if there's anything we can learn here,
it's that no matter if you're a student, an

00:11:47.820 --> 00:11:53.690
office worker, or a researcher with the SCP
Foundation, think twice about cutting corners.

00:11:53.690 --> 00:11:59.270
It might save you a little bit of time and
money in the short term, but in the long term,

00:11:59.270 --> 00:12:01.470
the results could be fatal.

00:12:01.470 --> 00:12:08.260
Now go check out “SCP - 087 - The Stairwell”
and “SCP-035 - The Possessive Mask” for

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:11.699
more explanations of the creepiest SCP tales.

